Maintainer request (2026-09-27): adding Getty/karr as a source should offer its .claude/skills/* for install. Getty/karr publishes nothing under skills/ – its skills, agents and rules sit in the Claude project layout: .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md (+ references/, scripts/), .claude/agents/<name>.md, .claude/rules/<name>.md, all committed.

Design (decided by the coordinator):
- catalog.scan also reads .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md[.njk], .claude/agents/<name>.md[.njk], .claude/rules/<name>.md[.njk]. Install target is unchanged (skills/<name>/, agents/<name>.md, rules/<name>.md), whatever the source path.
- Precedence: skills/ agents/ rules/, then plugin.json skills, then .claude/. A .claude/ item whose name the published layout already holds is skipped silently – never an error (a repo often keeps an installed copy of its own skill there).
- .claude/ is best effort: what the published layout would reject there (a symlinked .claude, .claude/skills, item or file inside an item) skips that item or directory, never fails the scan. A source that scans today must scan the same way with its .claude/ tree added. Symlinks are still never followed.
- Not in scope: bundles under .claude/, .agents/skills (Codex layout), share/.

